<title>USA: N.J. tunnel project extends bid deadline -- paper.</title>
<headline>N.J. tunnel project extends bid deadline -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The three firms vying to build Atlantic City's $330 million tunnel project have received a three-week extension to submit bids for the contract, the Philadelphia Inquirer reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>The extension, requested by the companies, means bids are now due June 13 instead of May 23.</p>
<p>The tunnel has been at the center of a controversy involving Trump Hotels &amp; Casinos Inc, which contends the state's financial support for the project gives rival casino developers an unfair advantage and violates state law.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
</text>
